# A tour of Aethrion

```elixir
Mix.install([
  # From a checkout of this repository; use {:aethrion, github: "simulacre7/aethrion"} elsewhere.
  {:aethrion, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.14"}
])
```

## A world

A world is plain data: characters and directed relationships. `demo_state/0` gives Mina, Yuna, and Haru; here we build our own small office.

```elixir
alias Aethrion.{Character, Event, Explain, Relationship, State}

world =
  State.new(
    characters: [
      %Character{id: "ana", name: "Ana", profile: "New on the team."},
      %Character{id: "ben", name: "Ben", profile: "Ana's desk neighbour.", traits: [:calm]},
      %Character{id: "cho", name: "Cho", profile: "Ben's oldest friend.", traits: [:talkative]}
    ],
    relationships: [
      %Relationship{from: "ana", to: "user", affinity: 30, trust: 20},
      %Relationship{from: "ben", to: "user", affinity: 30, trust: 25},
      %Relationship{from: "ben", to: "ana", affinity: 35, trust: 30},
      %Relationship{from: "cho", to: "user", affinity: 30, trust: 25},
      %Relationship{from: "cho", to: "ana", affinity: 25, trust: 20},
      %Relationship{from: "ana", to: "cho", affinity: 30, trust: 45}
    ]
  )
```

## Something happens

The user snaps at Ana while Ben is at the next desk. Everything that follows comes from rules.

```elixir
{:ok, step} =
  Aethrion.step(
    world,
    Event.message_sent("user", "ana", "This is wrong again.", tone: :hostile, observed_by: ["ben"])
  )

Enum.each(step.log, &IO.puts/1)
```

Each character line is an output with deterministic text (a model can rephrase it later):

```elixir
for %{text: text} = output <- step.outputs, Aethrion.Output.expressive?(output) do
  "#{output.character_id} -> #{output.to}: #{text}"
end
```

## Why?

Every change is traced. Why does Ben trust the user less?

```elixir
[step]
|> Explain.relationship("ben", "user", :trust)
|> Explain.describe()
```

## Time passes, news travels

Ana, upset, confides in Cho, who trusts Ana's word. A few more events, then a week.

```elixir
{:ok, world, steps} =
  Aethrion.run(step.state, [
    Event.message_sent("user", "ana", "Nobody asked for your opinion.", tone: :hostile, observed_by: ["ben"]),
    Event.time_tick("that evening", hours: 3),
    Event.message_sent("user", "ben", "Coffee?", tone: :warm),
    Event.time_tick("next week", hours: 120)
  ])

for step <- steps, %{type: :bond_changed} = change <- step.outputs do
  "#{change.from} toward #{change.to}: #{change.before} -> #{change.after}"
end
```

What Ben has come to believe about the user, once the details faded:

```elixir
for memory <- world.memories, memory.character_id == "ben", memory.kind == :impression do
  memory.content
end
```

## See it as a page

A scenario is the same world and events as JSON-friendly data; a report renders it.

```elixir
scenario_data = %{
  "name" => "Tour",
  "world" => world |> State.to_data(),
  "events" => [Event.message_sent("user", "ben", "Sorry about the other day.", tone: :warm) |> Event.to_data()]
}

{:ok, scenario} = Aethrion.Scenario.from_data(scenario_data)
{:ok, result} = Aethrion.Scenario.run(scenario)

result |> Aethrion.Report.html() |> IO.iodata_to_binary() |> Kino.HTML.new()
```

